# Both images build from the PACKAGE ROOT (that is what keeps a single policy.yaml on disk), so
# the build context is this whole directory and everything not excluded here is one careless
# `COPY . /app` away from being inside an image.
#
# reference/ is the line that matters. reference/improvers/sanity_improver.py is a WORKING
# CANDIDATE SOLUTION to the benchmark task -- it implements the group-std mid-band recursion the
# sanity chain uses to prove the harness can register a gain at all. Shipping it to the agent
# would hand every submission a known-good improver and the benchmark would measure a `cp`.
# tests/contract_check.py fails the build if this entry is missing or if any Dockerfile COPYs
# from reference/, because an exclusion nobody checks is an exclusion that gets deleted.
reference/

# Chain outputs and staged assets never belong in an image either.
_harness_test/
chains/
environment/staged.lock.yaml

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
